<GuideLayout 
  title="High-Compression Fabrics: The Science of Performance Leggings" 
  type="FABRIC GUIDE"
  description="Analyze the blend of nylon and spandex that creates the perfect compression. Ideal for high-intensity training and professional gym wear."
>
  <h2>Why Fabric is Everything</h2>
  <p>In the activewear industry, the fabric is the product. For performance leggings, the goal is to achieve 'Zero Distraction'—a fit that feels secure, remains opaque (squat-proof), and manages moisture perfectly.</p>
  
  <h3>The Gold Standard: Nylon/Spandex Blends</h3>
  <p>Most premium performance leggings use a blend of 75% Nylon and 25% Spandex. Nylon provides superior durability and a cool-to-the-touch feel, while the high spandex content ensures the leggings retain their shape and provide 4-way stretch.</p>

  <h3>Technical Specifications to Watch</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>GSM (Grams per Square Meter):</strong> For squat-proof leggings, we recommend 260-300 GSM.</li>
    <li><strong>Interlock Knit:</strong> Unlike single jersey, interlock is a double-knit fabric that prevents 'grinning' (seeing the white spandex when stretched).</li>
    <li><strong>Moisture-Wicking Treatment:</strong> All our fabrics are treated with hydrophilic finishes that pull sweat away from the body to the surface of the fabric for fast evaporation.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Branding Your Fabric</h3>
  <p>At Fitclo, we can develop custom fabric hands (textures)—from peach-skin soft to sleek and shiny—allowing your brand to have a unique 'signature feel' that customers recognize immediately.</p>
</GuideLayout>
